{"title":"Magic Square Association","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Magic Square Association</b> (MSA) is an educational organization based in Hong Kong. It serves as the official regional manager and administrator for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Mathematics_Competitions\" title=\"American Mathematics Competitions\">American Mathematics Competitions</a> (AMC) exams—including the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8\" title=\"AMC 8\">AMC 8</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10\" title=\"AMC 10\">AMC 10</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12\" title=\"AMC 12\">AMC 12</a>—for students in Hong Kong and Macau. \n</p><p>In addition to hosting the official North American exam dates, the Magic Square Association coordinates with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_Association_of_America\" title=\"Mathematical Association of America\">Mathematical Association of America</a> (MAA) to administer secure, authorized alternate test papers (such as the Regional Version) to accommodate international time zones and maintain strict test integrity.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Magic_Square_Association&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Mathematics_Competitions\" title=\"American Mathematics Competitions\">American Mathematics Competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_(Regional)_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 (Regional) Problems\">2026 AMC 8 (Regional) Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018093929\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.007 seconds\nPreprocessor v